      "fieldValue": "Picture 1 is the exact opening frame and controls the clean five-person human-wall formation, 40mm right-front viewpoint, foreground shoulder framing, wet underground junction, layered spacing, and cyan-amber-red lighting. Picture 2 is Xiaoxin's identity and wardrobe reference: only the sharp large portrait controls the center lead's face; the blurred standing views control his body, black survival clothing, harness, gloves, boots, and left-forearm bandage. Picture 3 preserves the same four distinct rescued men and their individual outfits; use it only to lock the five-person cast, not to replace Picture 1's human-wall opening. Reference Audio 1 controls 136 BPM timing, Xiaoxin's Chinese singing timing only when his mouth is visible, and the final “三、二、一” choreography accents. Reference Audio 2 is an automatic duplicate of Reference Audio 1 and adds no independent instruction.\n\nCreate an eight-second cinematic, high-energy K-pop boy-group sequence with exactly five young East Asian men and three clearly edited shots. Xiaoxin remains the center lead and only singer, identified as (S1), singing <d>[Chinese] 不是不想把你们救，是我还没学会说不，当所有频道一起求救，三、二、一。</d> The group is under real pressure but moves with determined choreography: the human wall breaks open quickly, the final overhead section begins early and sustains a large, readable directional dance phrase. This is dance, never an attack.\n\n[Shot 1] From 00:00.000 to 00:01.400, begin exactly from Picture 1 in a 38mm full-body medium-wide shot about 35 degrees right-front. The two near dancers are foreground shoulder anchors, but on the very first beat they each make one forceful outward shoulder-and-forearm sweep and one quick side step, opening the central sightline. The two rear dancers answer with a low-to-high arm pull and grounded diagonal half-step. Xiaoxin is revealed before 00:01.000; he steps once into the gap, brings his bandaged left forearm across his sternum, and turns his torso toward the blue route. The camera makes a smooth, short forward dolly at constant speed; no body crosses another path.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:01.400, hard cut to a 55mm off-axis chest-to-knee medium shot. Keep one blurred dancer shoulder at each extreme edge but leave Xiaoxin's lower face mostly in three-quarter profile, never a prolonged frontal lip close-up. On “是我还没学会说不,” Xiaoxin executes one decisive two-count: a grounded forward rock with a chest hit, then a recoil with eyes breaking from the green radio light toward the red exit. The four dancers are visible behind and beside him in staggered levels, performing a fast, clean elbow-cannon from left to right plus one synchronized half-turn of their torsos toward their separate routes. The camera stays stable and moves only a small diagonal track.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:03.300, hard cut to a locked true vertical overhead wide shot with all five full bodies and the junction routes visible. Begin already in motion, not in a held spiral. On “当所有频道一起求救,” all five execute a full four-count route phrase: one grounded inward gather step, one hard outward heel-toe travel step, an arm carve from chest to assigned route, then a clean planted stop. On “三,” each dancer drops into one low, shallow lunge facing a different exit while Xiaoxin stays centered. On “二,” the four dancers take one additional brisk traveling step outward and strike an angular forearm line along their own body paths. On “一,” Xiaoxin drives one counter-step forward and raises a firm right stop palm while the four dancers snap their heads to their exits and freeze in a broken four-ray rupture. The final 0.8 second has only settling breath and wet-floor reflections, not a static pose held for multiple seconds.\n\nRequire immediate first-frame movement, continuous 136 BPM kinetic flow, clear footwork, sharp arm paths, strong but grounded levels, five distinct bodies, and clean anatomical separation. No slow reveal, pose counting, flat row, W, V, perfect diamond, equal spacing, complete orbit, jumping, spinning, zombie attack, grabbing, touching, body merging, extra arms, sixth person, cloned dancer, weapon, microphone, stage lights, camera shake, speed ramp, new stains, texture boiling, skin speckle, text, logo, or watermark. Reference Audio 1 is temporary guidance; restore the original master song in post-production.\n"
